st that look this is all  i have i don't want to give you the rest  of this because you know this is  privileged stuff  or  is there more that we don't know about  how much can we trust ali alexander  now of course that's a subjective thing  if it were me you know just personal  opinion here i don't think i would trust  him  i'm not on the committee i'm not a  lawyer i don't get to make that  determination all i can have is my  personal opinion of him which i just  gave you  so the committee  has a decision to make  do they  just say all right ollie if you're going  to sue us we don't want to get involved  in that whatever you've been a  cooperative person thank you very much  we've got what we need for now we'll  contact you if we need more  or do they fight it and say oh no we  think you've got something to hide  who knows where it goes from here but  honestly and this is something i was  saying since the early days of this  committee alexander should have been the  very first person they ever asked for  material from  i mean like i said he was the brainchild  of stop the steel you know  why was he not the first if your goal  was to find out what happened that day  why was the organizer of the rally not  the first person  you subpoenaed  to me that makes the committee look bad  that makes it look like they were on  some kind of political hunt  to go after other people first i mean  why was steve bannon  subpoenaed before the guy that organized  the rally that doesn't make sense to me  and just to play devil's advocate for a  moment  if i were alexander that is something i  would bring up in that lawsuit  so  just throwing that out there  but either way  if he has more information he should be  compelled to turn it over  if it's determined that he is being  honest then okay he shouldn't have to  turn anything else over  he's one of the few people let's be  honest that's actually agreed to go and  cooperate with this committee because he  says you know i don't want 